You've managed to get five characters to Astral without knowing how to 
deal with a stunning attack?

One basic strategy for Astral:

- Have low AC (-30 or better)
- Have 200+ HP
- Have potions of full healing, a blessed or enchanted unihorn, and 
amulets of life saving (if you don't have the amulet slot taken up by 
something more useful :-)
- Have several wands of teleport available
- Wear speed or jumping boots
- Use telepathy to check out which rider is where when you first get to 
Astral. Try to avoid the rider you're afraid of the most (i.e., do the 
other altars first.)
- DO NOT MELEE ANY MORE THAN NECESSARY!!!!!
- Use the wands of teleport to get monsters out of the way.
- Slip through the open spaces. Use your turns to move, not fight. Speed 
boots will allow you to get more moves; jumping boots will allow you to 
move more than one space per turn. Your call.
- Focus on getting to the altars. Nothing else matters (except, 
obviously, keeping yourself alive).
- If possible, take riders out from a distance. If you have to melee, 
try to kill them quick--they have strong attacks, but are low on HP. 
This is one case in which it's sometimes better to get in one more hit 
before curing yourself.

